1. d4 Nf6 2. Bg5 c5 3. d5 d6 4. Nc3 h6!? {A little-played idea which may be quite good. Mason's approach is combative; he will not let Gormally win by technical play alone.} 5. Bxf6 (5. Bh4 g5 6. Bg3 Nh5 7. e4 Nxg3 8. hxg3 Bg7 {is nothing at all for White. The knight on c3 is in the wrong place:} 9. Qd2 a6 10. a4 Qa5 11. Nd1 Qxd2+ 12. Kxd2 e6 13. Ne3 Kd8 14. c3 Nd7 15. dxe6 fxe6 16. f4 Kc7 $15 17. Nf3 Nf6 18. Bd3 g4 19. Nh4 h5 20. Rhf1 Rd8 21. Kc2 b6 22. Rae1 Bb7 23. Nd1 Bc6 24. b3 b5 25. Nb2 c4 26. bxc4 bxa4 27. e5 Ne8 28. Be4 dxe5 29. Bxc6 Kxc6 30. Nxa4 Nd6 31. Nb2 Rab8 32. Ng6 e4 33. f5 Rxb2+ 34. Kxb2 Nxc4+ 35. Kc2 Rd2+ 36. Kb3 Kb5 {0-1 Walton,A (2137)-Knott,S (2348)/England 2010/CB03_2010}) 5... exf6 6. e4 f5?! {Very risky indeed, but I think Mason is angry about his pulled hamstring suffered in the ECF cricket match. He wants to demolish Gormally as if he were a member of the opposing University of Kent staff team.} (6... g6 7. Nf3 Bg7 8. Be2 O-O 9. O-O f5 $132) 7. Bb5+ Nd7 8. exf5 Be7 9. Nge2 a6 10. Bxd7+ Bxd7 11. Ng3 Bf6 {The scene is set. Two bishops vs two knights, but White has an extra pawn.} 12. Nce4 ({Maybe White could just play it safe and castle now and this does seem rather better for him:} 12. O-O O-O 13. Qf3 Be5 14. Rfe1 $16) 12... Bxb2 13. Nxd6+ Ke7 14. Rb1 (14. Nge4! {is an excellent move:} Bxa1 (14... Qa5+ 15. Kf1 Be5 16. Qe2!! Bxa1 (16... Bb5 17. Nxb5 Bxa1 18. d6+ Kf8 19. Nc7 Rb8 20. Qc4 Qb4 21. Qxb4 cxb4 22. Ke2 Be5 23. Rd1 Rd8 24. Rd5 Bc3 25. Nc5 b6 26. Na4 Rg8 27. g3 $18) 17. Nxc5+ Kf8 18. Nxd7+ Kg8 19. Nxf7 Qxd5 20. Nxh8 Qxd7 21. Ng6 Re8 22. Qc4+ Kh7 23. g4 $18) 15. Qxa1 Qa5+ 16. Ke2 (16. Kd1) 16... Kf8 17. f6 Rh7 18. Qe5 $18) 14... Kxd6 15. Ne4+ Kc7 16. d6+ Kc8 17. O-O Bd4 18. c3 Bc6 19. Qd3 Qh4 ({So far, so good, but now} 19... Re8! {was strongest:} 20. Rbe1 (20. Rfe1 Bb5 21. Rxb5 axb5 22. cxd4 c4 23. Qb1 Ra5 $15) 20... Bb5 21. c4 Bc6 $19) 20. Rfe1 Be5 21. g3 Qh3 22. Qe3 Qxf5 (22... Rd8 23. Qxc5 Bxd6 24. Nxd6+ Rxd6 25. f3! $18) 23. Qxc5 Qd7 24. Qxe5 Re8 25. Qc5 $16 {The assessment of the position has changed completely and with Mason in time-trouble, there is no advice to offer Black.} Re6 26. Nd2 Qxd6 27. Qxd6 Rxd6 28. Nc4 Kc7 29. Nxd6 Kxd6 30. Rbd1+ Kc5 31. Rd4 Re8 32. Rxe8 Bxe8 33. f4 Bc6 34. Kf2 {The technical part of the game is handled very well by Gormally.} Bd5 35. a3 f5 36. Ke3 b5 37. h3 h5 38. a4 bxa4 39. Rxa4 Bc4 40. Ra1 g6 41. Kd2 Kd6 42. Re1 Bb5 43. Re5! {White's king gets to d4 and beyond, after which further resistance is pointless.} 1-0

